  "body": "Turning has no cutting-data model: no surface speed (Vc, m/min or SFM) or feed per revolution.\n\n**Where:** `crates/tools/src/cutting.rs` `TABLE` holds milling windows only, and `tabulated()` (`crates/app/src/cutting.rs:41`) excludes every lathe kind. A lathe tool's `rpm`/`feed` are a fixed spindle rpm and mm/min, which are the wrong units for turning, where speed depends on the working diameter.\n\n**Effect:** a lathe or mill-turn tool library has to carry placeholder values. Users enter turning data by hand per operation, with no suggestion. The posted program's S/F words (and G96/G95 where the post supports them, cf. #772) can't come from the tool.\n\n**Fix sketch:**\n- Turning rows in the cutting table: Vc and f/rev per work material, for HSS and carbide, as conservative handbook-range starting values like the milling rows.\n- Lathe tools store Vc + f/rev, with a max-rpm clamp.\n- Operations derive S/F, or G96/G95 on posts that state CSS.\n- Old files load unchanged.\n\nEffort: high, since it changes posted S/F words.\n\n**Done means:** a turning op on a known material gets a suggested Vc and f/rev; posted S/F (or G96/G95) match; pinned on a lathe post golden.\n",
